mapledmaaddr (#528) -- KILL TABLE 4 (TARGETED), PRETABLE, written 2026-09-12 BEFORE the table runs.  Post-table notes go
in a SEPARATE file (POSTTABLE.out).

WHY.  grok's §F2 answer named `fatal("\n");' -- a diagnostic printing only a BLANK line -- as a survivor.  The quiet
grammar admits `^$' and table 3's accounting counted hex / put / disassembly lines only.  Same §F2 ask as table 3's legs
(the cap counts asks, not findings); the detector is unshipped, so the repair is L1 construction on a FLOOR channel
(interval silence, Fable pass 1).

THE CHANGE -- noise() only; no row, no session, no value changed; still 35 rows, twelve read sessions.  Added to the
table-3 checks, each MEASURED on the clean build first (blank_measure.py here, 3 reps x 3 read sessions, build/gxemul
at the fix: every session `blanks=1 CR=LF=CRLF bareCR=0', the single empty element being the one after the final
newline):
    interior blank lines   want 0   (the grammar's `^$' member no longer licenses a diagnostic's blank line)
    bare CR                want 0   (every CR in a clean pty transcript is the CRLF of onlcr)
    prompt lines           want len(cmds)  (a `GXemul> ' line is owed once per command; the typed `quit' echo is NOT
                           counted, because it may miss the read window on a loaded host)
Re-measured after the change: 35/35 CONTROL=OK (BASE_prelaunch.out, from _scratchpad/maple_base35b.out).

WHY A TARGETED TABLE AND NOT A FULL ONE.  The new noise() is a SUPERSET of table 3's: every earlier condition is kept
and three are added, so for every table-3 leg `read silent' can only stay red or turn red, and no value row can change.
No table-3 kill can become an escape; the only failure a stricter check can introduce is a FALSE RED on the fix, which
BASE measures.  So: BASE, HEAD, the three new diagnostic shapes, and the three shapes table 3 already killed on this
channel (verbatim, bare hex, and an exit's deficit) as regression legs for the channel itself.

INSTRUMENT: maple_dmaaddr_probe.FROZEN4.py, copied at launch.  BASELINE: SEC (the fix).  MUTATOR: mut_maple4.py (table
3's plus M_BLANKDIAG, M_CRDIAG, M_PROMPTDIAG; each dry-run against SEC, one-line diff read before this block).

PREDICTIONS (score / 35):
  BASE           35/35 CONTROL=OK
  HEAD           11/35  as table 3 (24 failing, read silent among them)
  M_KEEPFATAL    34/35  read silent alone (off-grammar line)
  M_HEXDIAG      34/35  read silent alone (hex surplus)
  M_EXITONLY     11/35  as table 3 (read silent by the deficit)
  M_BLANKDIAG    34/35  read silent alone -- `interior blank lines 1, commands owe 0' per read
  M_CRDIAG       34/35  read silent alone -- `bare CR lines 1, commands owe 0' per read (the CR lands before the next
                        prompt; after CR-stripping that line is a normal prompt line, so ONLY the bare-CR count sees it)
  M_PROMPTDIAG   34/35  read silent alone -- `prompt lines N+1, commands owe N' (a `GXemul> ' line is grammar-legal)

CHANNEL -- each new leg names the one count that must differ; each count is exact on the clean build (measured), so
each channel varies under its mutant by construction.  CLAIM -> ROW: the CONTRACT's new clause (blank line, bare carriage
return, prompt-shaped line) maps to `read silent' and these three legs.
